  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "The requested mean-velocity and intrinsic sig_v grids are now represented without changing any V14 count, mean-velocity, observer, split, or target value.",
    "Native sig_v is physically nontrivial, but a fixed source-balanced linear control finds less than one percent common-domain validation improvement and essentially no unique gain beyond the dispersion lower bound already encoded by neighboring retained means.",
    "Intrinsic sig_v must remain distinct from propagated observational sigma of the mean in the future CF4 interface, but sig_v alone does not justify another full generative training run.",
    "V32 summarized each 3x3x3 neighborhood by mean and standard deviation and therefore did not test oriented patch sufficiency. The next audit must use the full oriented multiscale patch with a frozen nonlinear learner before changing the residual generator."
